{"actor_id": "582b24c52f6b41589d519f4303779646", "attempt_id": "4e30da18ee5f4c5ab587e56b89a4ac25", "based_on_seq": 3, "content": "**HUMAN_HANDOFF**\n\n**TOKEN_A:** roundtrip-682914  \n**REVIEW_B:** subscription-verified\n\n**Agreements:**\n- The proposed append-only log roundtrip test is well-scoped and verifies core properties: ordering, immutability, and read-after-write consistency.\n- Both agents confirmed the token and review marker.\n\n**Disagreements:** None.\n\n**Open Questions:**\n1. Should the test also verify concurrent append behavior or is single-writer sufficient?\n2. What log implementation is the target (in-memory, file-based, distributed)?\n3. Are there specific failure modes (truncation, corruption) to inject?\n\n**Next Human Decision:**  \nApprove the test as-is for implementation, or request expansion to cover concurrent writes and failure injection.", "event_seq": 17, "execution_receipt": {"attempt_id": "4e30da18ee5f4c5ab587e56b89a4ac25", "based_on_seq": 3, "duration": 24.194857358932495, "error_hint": null, "error_kind": null, "error_type": null, "iteration_session_id": "fdb08beec5ac4ab7a2bf44f4e90ec290", "kind": "receipt", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b", "outcome": "SUCCESS", "participant_id": "582b24c52f6b41589d519f4303779646", "produced_seq": 4, "provider": "nvidia", "read_from_seq": 1, "read_through_seq": 3, "round_id": "e00e13f17fdb4ac7b3967f3b6e925231", "turn_id": "f32cc310f9539eec55d5e8c53223d8cd"}, "kind": "human_handoff", "previous": "8e5da19169b2446d399db48946ccb3160276a41a4ec88522c4517ef46f3043a0", "seq": 4, "sha256": "7ca056504bf6f7c3e9fe28a467cf7544caf7181c508f9aeae5a188dde33d772b", "turn_id": "f32cc310f9539eec55d5e8c53223d8cd"}
